+## Interfaces
+
+Three components expose new or modified public boundaries; all others are internal rewrites. Shell function signatures use positional-arg notation; return codes are POSIX (0 = success, 1 = failure).
+
+### `tests/helpers/skill-markdown.bash` -- `extract_section_fence_aware`
+
+The new fence-aware extraction function is a sibling to `extract_section` and shares the same empty-extract diagnostic convention.
+
+```bash
+# extract_section_fence_aware(file, start_pattern)
+#
+# $1  file        -- path to the Markdown file to extract from
+# $2  start_pattern -- grep -E compatible pattern matching the anchor line
+#                      (e.g. "^### Review Round")
+#
+# Output: all lines from the first start_pattern match through
+#         the next out-of-fence heading line ("^## " or "^### ") or EOF,
+#         with fence state tracked (``` toggle) so heading-shaped lines
+#         inside code fences are NOT treated as section boundaries.
+#         The anchor line itself IS included in the output.
+#
+# Returns: 0 on non-empty extract, written to stdout
+#          1 with "skill-markdown: <file>: <start_pattern>: empty extract"
+#            diagnostic to stderr on empty or missing extract
+#
+# Bash 3.2 portable; no nameref, no associative arrays, no $'...'
+extract_section_fence_aware()
+```
+
+### `scripts/run-codex-review.sh` -- `detect_host` and `check_codex_available`
+
+The two host-detection functions are the single shared probe implementation serving both G6 (transport selection) and G7b (model_routing default selection) per DKR10.
+
+```bash
+# detect_host()
+#
+# Probes COPILOT_CLI=1 first; falls through to "claude-code" default.
+# Codex CLI as a host is out of scope for v0.7.1 and falls through
+# to the "claude-code" branch.
+#
+# Output: "copilot-cli" or "claude-code" written to stdout
+# Returns: always 0
+# No arguments.
+detect_host()
+
+# check_codex_available(host)
+#
+# $1  host -- "copilot-cli" or "claude-code" (output of detect_host)
+#
+# Under "copilot-cli": Codex is always available as gpt-5.3-codex
+#   via the native task tool; no filesystem probe; returns 0.
+# Under "claude-code": globs
+#   ~/.claude/plugins/cache/openai-codex/codex/*/scripts/codex-companion.mjs;
+#   returns 0 on at least one match, 1 on no match.
+#
+# Returns: 0 (Codex reachable on this host), 1 (not reachable)
+check_codex_available()
+```
+
+### `scripts/run-third-party-llm.sh` -- `_control_char_check`
+
+The internal helper replaces the inline `grep -qP` call within the security pre-flight block; it is not exported for external callers.
+
+```bash
+# _control_char_check(str)
+#
+# $1  str -- the string to inspect (a single header name or header value)
+#
+# Strips all POSIX [:cntrl:] bytes (0x00--0x1F and 0x7F, including LF)
+# using LC_ALL=C tr -d '[:cntrl:]', then compares byte count via
+# LC_ALL=C wc -c.  A non-zero difference means at least one control
+# byte was present.
+#
+# Returns: 0 (clean -- no control bytes), 1 (control byte detected)
+# On rc=1, the caller invokes die() with the header-validation message.
+_control_char_check()
+```
